# Microphone Dictation and Computer Audio Together

Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: M2-M4 Required input extension
Dependencies: 19_LIVE_TRANSCRIPTION.todo, 22_NATIVE_PYTHON_RUNTIME.todo

## Purpose

Transcribe dictated chat questions through the selected microphone while retaining selected computer audio,
without reading chat applications or requiring Docker/cloud inference.

## Tasks

- [x] Record explicit owner microphone authorization and supersession of earlier computer-only scope.
- [x] Define Computer/Mic/Both, explicit Start, separate source labels and v1-compatible v2 protocol.
- [x] Implement two independent native inputs and bounded source-tagged PCM transport.
- [x] Implement independent Python recognizers, source partials/timing and global final IDs in one session.
- [x] Add input selectors/meters and labelled transcript/export with no silent source substitution.
- [x] Preserve cancellation, stop/final drain, device-loss cleanup and no automatic mic startup.
- [x] Handle stale owned idle service upgrade without interrupting active transcription.
- [x] Run deterministic/native/backend/UI and real-recognizer synthetic dual-source integration.
- [x] Record manual microphone/device/echo/OS-indicator and actual capture qualification limits.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Computer, Mic and Both behave explicitly; capture begins only after Start and protocol readiness.
- [ ] Source finals do not erase the other partial; export preserves source labels and unfinished text.
- [ ] Missing/denied/lost requested input stops the session, never substitutes or quietly downgrades.
- [ ] No real microphone recording, playback, chat access or upload is used by unattended tests.
- [ ] Windows mic privacy indicators and acoustic echo are disclosed without invisibility/AEC guarantees.

